    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 31.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf he betihtlod weorðe ⁊ he ut oðhleape, gilde se hlaford þæs mannes were ðam cingce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-a">And gif he betyhled weorðe ⁊ he ut hleape, gylde se hlaford þæs mannes were þam cyninge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-q">Quodsi accusetur et fugiat, reddat dominus eius regi weram (id est pretium natiuitatis) hominis illius.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="31a.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ gyf he betyhtlod weorðe ⁊ he ut ætleape, gylde se hlaford ðæs mannes wér ðam cynge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf he betihtlod weorðe and he ut oðhleape, gilde se hlaford þæs mannes were ðam cingce. And gyf man þone hlaford teo, þæt he be his ræde ut hleope, ladige hine mid V þegnum, and beo him sylf syxta.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if he is accused and escapes, the lord shall pay his (the man's) wergeld to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if he comes to be accused and escapes, the lord is to pay the fugitive’s wergild to the king. And if the lord is accused of advising him to escape, he must exonerate himself with the support of five thanes, and himself will make the sixth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if he is accused and he escapes, the lord is to pay the man’s wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn er angeklagt wird, er jedoch hinaus entflieht, zahle der Herr dem König das Wergeld dieses Untergebenen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if he is accused but escapes, let the lord pay the king the wergild of that man.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="335"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-11">I Atr 1.11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1, 11</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_52-1">Leis Wl 52.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-11">I Atr 1.11–13</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 31:1-2: I Atr 1:11-13</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Atr 1.11.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">oðhleape: ætleape B; leape A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">man: hi B</note>
      </div>
